  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"Ten original color lithographs by Lois Long, life-size illustrations of fifteen species. Ten lithographs by John Cage in handwriting using superimpositions of five graded lithographic pencils."--Leaf [1].</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"Signed and numbered by the artists in an edition of seventy-five, ten artist proofs Roman-numbered, five presentation proofs, and some trial proof singles."--Leaf [1].</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"The lithographs were drawn by artists John Cage and Lois Long and handprinted at Hollanders Workshop, Inc. During August '71 to May 1972, twelve stones and fifty-nine aluminum plates were prepared and printed by Fred Genis ... on white Arches cover 22 1/2 x 30 inches, old and new watermark .... All stones and plates have been effaced"--Leaf [1].</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">John Cage's texts together with botanical statements by Alexander H. Smith are printed on 10 transparent Japanese papers which overlay the mushroom illustrations by Lois Long.</subfield>
  </datafield>
